For a launch, I can't afford to under-sell, so I need a mechanism that works without requiring a timely sweeper. One idea is to use time-bucketed counters, maintaining reserved quantities in buckets by expiration minute—perhaps 10 buckets. When reserving, I'd add quantities to the bucket corresponding to the expiry time, and available inventory would equal total minus sold minus the sum of the current buckets for the last 10 minutes. This way, expired reservations drop out automatically, and I wouldn’t need a sweeper—this feels like an elegant solution! It’s crucial to ensure only one writer updates the reservation while maintaining strong transactions.
thinking
