If there's another reserve made at minute T+1, it uses expiry = T+11, which refers to a different index. Only at minute T+10 do reserves use expiry = T+20, affecting the same index as an earlier reservation's expiry of T+10. 

At T+10, a new reserve could reset the bucket due to differing epoch and expiry minutes, but that's fine since older reservations just expired. However, if a checkout for a reservation expiring at T+10 happens at minute T+9.5, the bucket hasn't been reset yet. 

